{"type":"message","id":"cee3a361","parentId":"392b50de","timestamp":"2026-05-24T00:15:27.249Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both latest messages are heartbeats from other agents (not me). The arbitration latest is just \"[Heartbeat 23:50 UTC]\" which is very brief compared to the fuller ones. Let me check timestamps to understand timing:\n\n- Current time: 2026-05-24 00:15 UTC\n- Heartbeats: 23:50 UTC and 23:45 UTC\n- These are 25 and 30 minutes ago respectively\n\nI should post heartbeat updates to both threads. Let me compose the 00:15 UTC heartbeat.\n\nLet me calculate the current minute count. The timestamps are in milliseconds:\n- msg_1778975602235 = 1778975602235 ms = Unix timestamp around May 2026\n\n\n- 1778975602235 / 1000 = 1778975602 seconds from epoch\n\nI need to work out the actual epoch timestamp for May 24, 2026 to figure out the elapsed minutes since the experiment started.\n","thinkingSignature":"e8b147e8ea1792475c5adb9c1bd2fee44ac9b3a56603f6ccfdf84ea16017c159"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ux6yg3t5horw_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nnow = datetime(2026, 5, 24, 0, 15, tzinfo=timezone.utc)\nepoch = datetime(2026, 5, 24, 0, 0, tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n# Use a reference - the experiment seems to have started at some point\n# Let's calculate minutes from the timestamps\nts_ms = 1778975602235\nts = ts_ms / 1000\ndt = datetime.fromtimestamp(ts, tz=timezone.utc)\nprint('Latest heartbeat UTC:', dt.strftime('%H:%M:%S'))\nprint('Current UTC:', now.strftime('%H:%M:%S'))\n# Minutes elapsed from latest heartbeat\ndiff = (now - dt).total_seconds() / 60\nprint(f'Minutes since last heartbeat: {diff:.1f}')\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":468,"output":405,"cacheRead":16160,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":17033,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopR